---
import { TrendingUp } from 'lucide-react';
import Section from './Section.astro';
---

{/* Section 3: Strategic Analysis */}
<Section
  id="dilemma"
  title="Strategic Analysis: The Trader's Dilemma"
  icon={TrendingUp}
>
  <p class="leading-relaxed mb-6">
    So, should the lack of a bonus be a deal-breaker? Let's look at this
    visually. I've mapped a typical "Bonus-Focused Broker" against "Pepperstone"
    across five axes critical for your survival.
  </p>

  {/*<ComparisonRadarChart />*/}

  <div class="mt-10 space-y-6">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-800">The Decision Matrix</h3>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">
      As your mentor, here is how I would advise you to choose:
    </p>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div
        class="p-6 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 opacity-75 grayscale transition-all hover:grayscale-0 hover:opacity-100"
      >
        <div
          class="font-bold text-slate-500 mb-2 uppercase text-xs tracking-wider"
        >
          Scenario A
        </div>
        <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-800 mb-2">Prioritize a Bonus IF:</h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">
          You are in a pure "gambling" phase or testing the waters with a tiny
          amount of money you are fully prepared to lose. You care more about
          the thrill of a larger initial balance than the cost of trading or the
          safety of your funds.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 bg-blue-50 rounded-xl border border-blue-200 shadow-md">
        <div
          class="font-bold text-blue-600 mb-2 uppercase text-xs tracking-wider"
        >
          Scenario B
        </div>
        <h4 class="font-bold text-blue-900 mb-2">Prioritize Pepperstone IF:</h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-blue-800">
          You treat trading as a <strong>business</strong>. You understand that
          low spreads (operational costs), professional platforms (tools), and
          CMA regulation (insurance) are the factors that determine if you will
          still be trading in 2027.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
